{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01287",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 4.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Come in, have a seat by the desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.6,
      "end_seconds": 10.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I mean, uh, good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.07,
      "end_seconds": 18.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Mm, hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.88,
      "end_seconds": 23.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Did the receptionist sort you out quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.54,
      "end_seconds": 29.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Let me think, yes, she was lovely about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.26,
      "end_seconds": 33.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 34.61,
      "end_seconds": 42.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, it's a dry cough in the evenings. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.17,
      "end_seconds": 46.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Alright, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.71,
      "end_seconds": 57.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "It's been like this since yesterday. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.61,
      "end_seconds": 68.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.19,
      "end_seconds": 82.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly. Only antihistamine, and it's not much. Pollen season definitely sets it off. I had sneezing fits before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.28,
      "end_seconds": 90.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.26,
      "end_seconds": 104.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.12,
      "end_seconds": 141.69,
      "duration_seconds": 18.57,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 15, pressure 117 over 73, height 162 centimetres. And SpO2 98 percent on room air, weight 80 kilos, pulse is 86 beats a minute, BMI works out to 30.5, temperature is 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.17,
      "end_seconds": 146.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Yeah, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.0,
      "end_seconds": 151.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.99,
      "end_seconds": 169.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "How about shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.39,
      "end_seconds": 174.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Nope, no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.21,
      "end_seconds": 177.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Any wheeze or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.69,
      "end_seconds": 183.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Um, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.34,
      "end_seconds": 187.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.25,
      "end_seconds": 191.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Um, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.75,
      "end_seconds": 196.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.32,
      "end_seconds": 204.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.76,
      "end_seconds": 209.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.13,
      "end_seconds": 219.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Well, um, I'm allergic to trimethoprim, I get itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.02,
      "end_seconds": 232.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.92,
      "end_seconds": 235.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.11,
      "end_seconds": 238.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Alright, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.87,
      "end_seconds": 242.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.72,
      "end_seconds": 247.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.08,
      "end_seconds": 252.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.81,
      "end_seconds": 255.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.86,
      "end_seconds": 261.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.42,
      "end_seconds": 265.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.06,
      "end_seconds": 273.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Low haemoglobin, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.24,
      "end_seconds": 284.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Listening to the whole story, I'd lean towards seasonal hay fever causing the cough. Early asthma is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.31,
      "end_seconds": 288.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Okay, so is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.81,
      "end_seconds": 299.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's seasonal hay fever causing the cough, and we'll watch how it goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.44,
      "end_seconds": 343.06,
      "duration_seconds": 27.62,
      "text": "You'll be taking fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That's for hay fever. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Keep windows closed on high-pollen days and wash your hair at night. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.26,
      "end_seconds": 362.2,
      "duration_seconds": 14.94,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if you start wheezing. If that happens, go to emergency. Come back in a month. Okay, anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.74,
      "end_seconds": 366.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "That's clear, um, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.35,
      "end_seconds": 369.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}